# Measurements are the evidence for the report's Experiments chapter and are
# small text files -- they stay versioned. Training logs in particular cannot be
# reproduced: --seed fixes the arenas, not the agent's exploration RNG.
# Figures are pure functions of the CSVs, so they are not worth versioning.
results/figures/

# Rung-2 training logs. Committed up to 29e56be, then removed: a 100 000-episode
# sweep is ~140 MB and they are reproducible from the commit plus the BM_* arm
# variables (E12 verified this by rerunning a sweep to identical results). The
# evaluations -- 35 KB each, and the actual evidence -- stay versioned.
# `results/train_local/` is the untracked archive of what was removed.
results/train_local/
results/train/task2_crates/*.csv
results/train/task2_crates/*.meta.json
results/train/task3_opponents/*.csv
results/train/task3_opponents/*.meta.json

# Local PyTorch resume snapshots contain replay/optimizer/RNG state and can be
# larger than GitHub's per-file limit. They are only needed to continue an
# interrupted local run; final models and compact training CSVs remain tracked.
results/train/ben_task4/*__training_state.pt

final_project.pdf

# stdout of parallel training sweeps; the training CSV is the record
logs/*.out

# Local working notes and one-off analysis scripts. Versioned during development
# and removed from the tree before publishing; the ledgers' references to
# scratchpad/ paths resolve in the history before that commit.
scratchpad/

# Per-run Q-tables from parallel training (BM_MODEL_SUFFIX). The real model is
# q_table.npy and stays versioned; these are scratch and must never end up in
# the submitted agent folder.
agent_code/*/q_table_*.npy

# Third-party agents installed under agent_code/ so the framework's loader can find
# them (agents.py:204 imports agent_code.<name>.callbacks), used only as opponents.
# Never committed: most of the source repos carry no LICENSE. The repo URLs and
# commit hashes are listed in the report.
agent_code/ext_*/

# Where those per-run tables now live. The submission is a zip of
# agent_code/<agent>/, so 700 MB of checkpoints sitting beside callbacks.py was
# a submission accident waiting to happen -- they are out of that folder
# entirely rather than merely ignored. Reproducible from the commit plus the
# BM_* variables in each run's .meta.json, so they are never versioned.
checkpoints/*
!checkpoints/benedict_task2/
checkpoints/benedict_task2/*
# ...with one exception. The shipped table is warm-started from this 12 800-row
# parent, and the parent belongs to the *pre-E20* feature map, so it cannot be
# retrained at HEAD -- without it in the repo, `q_table.npy` is not reproducible
# from a clone at all. 614 KB, and it is an input to the submitted model.
!checkpoints/benedict_task2/q_table_e16_c5_k03_s0__ep100000.npy
# ...and its layout sidecar, without which warm_start can only warn that the
# append-only assumption is unchecked instead of enforcing it.
!checkpoints/benedict_task2/q_table_e16_c5_k03_s0__ep100000.npy.layout.json

# Same exception for the rung-4 parent, and for a stronger reason: the claim
# above that checkpoints are "reproducible from the commit plus the BM_*
# variables" is FALSE from rung 3 on. main.py does not seed the provided
# opponents, and audit 5 established that no E30-E33 run passed
# --seed either, so two runs of the same command give different tables -- E31's
# suicide rate is bimodal across replications of an identical configuration.
# This file is therefore an *input* to the submitted agent, not an output of a
# recorded command: agent_code/benedict_task4/q_table.npy is a byte-identical
# copy of it (E33 arm ctl, seed 104, 20 000 episodes; selected on validation
# seed 550731 at won 0.382 and confirmed on ship seed 990731 at 0.372).
!checkpoints/benedict_task4/
checkpoints/benedict_task4/*
!checkpoints/benedict_task4/q_table_e33_ctl_s104__ep20000.npy

# E37 replaced the above as the shipped table, and needs two files for the same
# reason. The checkpoint is what agent_code/benedict_task4/q_table.npy is a
# byte-identical copy of (arm PLB2, seed 106, 20 000 episodes; selected on
# validation seed 550731 and confirmed on ship seed 990731 at score 3.949 /
# won 0.406, paired +0.255 [+0.039, +0.475] against the E33 table above).
# The parent is the warm start train.py loads by default, so without it a
# training run at the documented defaults starts from a different initial
# condition than the shipped table did -- which is exactly the confound audit 8
# found in E36.
!checkpoints/benedict_task4/q_table_e37_PLB2_s106__ep20000.npy
!checkpoints/benedict_task4/q_table_e37_PLB2_s106__ep20000.npy.layout.json
!checkpoints/benedict_task4/q_table_parent.npy
!checkpoints/benedict_task4/q_table_parent.npy.layout.json

# Local data and an unpublished test agent, not part of this repository.
data/
agent_code/benedict_cnn/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# The report (LaTeX source snapshot from Overleaf, section drafts, compiled
# previews). final_project.pdf forbids uploading the report to the repo, so this
# folder is never versioned; Overleaf is the source of truth.
report/
